+### CI
+
+`.github/workflows/specs.yml` runs the whole suite on every pull request. It builds the place from
+`ci.project.json`, a copy of `default.project.json` generated in the job with
+`ServerScriptService.LoadStringEnabled` on (Jest needs `loadstring` on a game server), saves the
+build as a new version of a dedicated CI place, and runs `ci/run-specs.luau` in that version
+through Open Cloud Luau Execution (`ci/run_luau_task.py`). The job fails when any spec fails or
+fails to load. It needs the repository secrets `ROBLOX_UNIVERSE_ID`, `ROBLOX_PLACE_ID`, and
+`ROBLOX_API_KEY` (scopes `universe-places:write` and
+`universe.place.luau-execution-session:write`). Specs run there on a server, so
+`RunService:IsServer()` is true, unlike in Studio's edit mode.
+
 ## Checks
 
 Tools come from Rokit (`rokit.toml`). Run each command on its own from the project root:
